theo-pod (t-169): clamp the TNS filter bottom at band 0

get_tns() subtracts each filter length from top without a floor. ISO/IEC
14496-3 takes bottom = max(top - length, 0); here a negative top went
through MINIMUM() into an unsigned start band, so the start coefficient
and the band count were garbage, and apply_tns() walked win_sfb_top[] and
coef[] past their ends. top is now clamped at 0. Found by the host fuzzer
(ASan global- and heap-buffer-overflow in apply_tns); regression input
tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-tns-negative-bottom.bin.

